WEBVTT

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:11.330
Mei, bring me the weak flour.

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:11.860
Okay!

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:13.200
Now the butter!

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.160
Okay!

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:15.740
Stir it until it turns creamy.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:16.450
Okay!

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:18.180
And thoroughly.

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:21.390
Want to go with a heart shape?

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:23.290
Which shape do you want, Mei?

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:26.450
Whatever you want.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.840
Just use something generic.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.020
How is that cute?

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:32.380
The oven's ready for you!

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:33.800
Thanks!

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:36.040
Tell me if I can help.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:38.370
I'm good at cooking.

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:39.480
Okay.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.170
She seems fun.

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:45.120
You look pretty different though.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.230
I sort of hope so.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:50.170
Next...

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:50.940
The powdered sugar.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:52.150
Oh, okay.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:53.620
Big brother...

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:54.870
How much longer?

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:56.290
Maybe thirty minut—

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:01.710
A lot more.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:04.290
Could you go somewhere else?

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:19.990
So what now?

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:30.440
Though my words yesterday

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:37.070
may have been lacking and passed you by

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:40.030
I will not give up

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:46.210
and try to understand you

00:01:51.830 --> 00:02:01.180
Sometimes I wish to be alone,

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:08.060
but even when I travel,

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:17.570
my heart remains uneasy and I realize whom I love

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:28.580
Daily life does not always turn out for the best,

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:31.920
but I will smile through it

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:42.300
I will always remember how happy I felt

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:48.310
when you told me

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:50.980
{part a}

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:28.560
Kai

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:28.560
No subject

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:28.560
I'm at the park right now. 

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.440
I'm at the park right now. 

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:11.390
At the park, my ass.

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:12.850
Over here!

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:14.680
'Sup!

00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:19.110
Guess you didn't see me.

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:25.060
Why are you laughing?

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:26.200
Sorry.

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.810
I just thought you looked the 
same as you did way back when.

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:30.790
It made me laugh.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:33.170
Take a closer look!

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:34.260
I changed plenty!

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:36.630
I started working out and I have a new hairstyle.

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:39.570
I guess the hairstyle wasn't intended.

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:42.830
Your brother practically forced it on me.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:45.380
I think it looks good.

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:46.550
Guess so.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:49.260
Truth be told, I sorta like it.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:54.560
I was afraid you'd forgotten about this place by now.

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:57.600
No way I would.

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:00.440
This'll always be our park.

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:06.030
Here we met, talked for the first time,

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:10.700
sat on the tire swing together and went down the slide.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:12.670
Feels like ancient history.

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:17.000
You're a blast from the past, though.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.100
Can it.

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:20.880
Playgrounds are a man's paradise.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.590
Here we can all be children again.

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:26.130
The purity of our hearts rises from—

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:27.040
I see. So that's why you love Land.

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:28.400
Yeah, exactly.

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:29.570
No!

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:31.870
The case with Land lies differently.

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:33.800
The appeal of Land is...

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.180
Sorry, bro.

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:36.960
Hey, listen to me!

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:50.830
Nice breeze.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:53.640
Yeah.

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:19.280
Hey, I've been wondering something for the longest time.

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:20.870
Mind if I ask?

00:06:20.870 --> 00:06:21.910
Why so ceremonious?

00:06:21.910 --> 00:06:22.900
Go ahead.

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:27.890
Back in middle school, I couldn't wait to get here.

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:31.440
I just hated school, you know?

00:06:33.130 --> 00:06:34.370
You were different.

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:39.420
You always had a crowd around you at school.

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:41.580
You seemed to be having a lot of fun.

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:43.540
But when I got here...

00:06:49.320 --> 00:06:53.550
I wondered why you'd come to this rundown playground.

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:54.860
It seemed so strange.

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:05.040
I see.

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:08.310
I never really thought about it.

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:12.440
I just liked this place.

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:14.360
That's all.

00:07:26.990 --> 00:07:28.050
Actually, you know,

00:07:29.020 --> 00:07:32.430
sometimes I felt like I was a chameleon or something.

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:38.950
Like something that changes its color to match its surroundings.

00:07:40.550 --> 00:07:46.760
I was kind of anxious that maybe I had no personality of my own outside of adjusting to others.

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:52.720
When I started feeling like that, I came here to lie on my back and look at the sky.

00:07:53.460 --> 00:07:55.700
It calmed me down.

00:07:56.460 --> 00:07:58.810
Maybe that's why I liked it.

00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:00.660
Yamato...

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:11.140
I used to hate this town.

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:12.860
Not anymore.

00:08:24.010 --> 00:08:25.510
I wonder what did it.

00:08:26.370 --> 00:08:28.490
Now it looks completely different to me.

00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:34.110
It's the same sight from up here, but the hate turned into affection.

00:08:34.790 --> 00:08:37.650
Now I have people I call friends.

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:43.000
Maybe having people around you does that just by itself.

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:47.420
I'm who I am now because I met you.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:52.010
You have your own personality, all right.

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:53.860
Anything else would be pretty sad.

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:56.800
This isn't just my opinion, but Tachibana's too.

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:25.560
When I met Mei and she told me she didn't need friends, I realized that I was sad myself.

00:09:27.010 --> 00:09:31.380
It felt like Mei filled some emptiness within me when that happened.

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:33.660
I'm glad I met her.

00:09:42.910 --> 00:09:45.200
You're a pretty simple guy!

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:48.070
Basically you were about to slit your wrists before you met her.

00:09:48.070 --> 00:09:50.160
It wasn't nearly that bad!

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:53.320
But man, I'm glad you've said how you feel.

00:09:58.670 --> 00:10:01.990
Damn, I know you lured me into this conversation.

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:25.680
<b>B{*\fax0.007}u{*\fax0.014}s {*\fax0.029}S{*\fax0.036}t{*\fax0.043}op</b>

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:25.680
<b>B{*\fax0.007}u{*\fax0.014}s {*\fax0.029}S{*\fax0.036}t{*\fax0.043}op</b>

00:10:45.230 --> 00:10:46.790
Hey, Kitagawa Megumi.

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:48.570
Not gonna get on?

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:02.190
Waiting for someone?

00:11:02.190 --> 00:11:03.680
None of your business.

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:10.700
Why're you sitting down?

00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:11.900
None of your business.

00:11:19.470 --> 00:11:21.330
Texting? A friend?

00:11:21.330 --> 00:11:22.190
Or your boyfriend?

00:11:24.460 --> 00:11:25.560
Since when d'you have a bo—

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:26.680
Just my friend.

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:28.550
She'll be here in five minutes or something.

00:11:28.550 --> 00:11:30.050
Talk to me to pass the time.

00:11:30.050 --> 00:11:32.020
Wouldn't know what to talk about.

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:33.130
Shut up or I'll kill you.

00:11:33.550 --> 00:11:35.210
You broad.

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:36.590
Hey, Momo!

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:37.520
What—

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:39.550
Sewing?

00:11:39.870 --> 00:11:41.120
Again?

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:42.000
Okay, sure!

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:43.260
Sounds good.

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:44.590
See you soon.

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:47.880
You got a problem?

00:11:47.880 --> 00:11:52.620
Nah, just surprised you can sound friendly.

00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:55.670
Be nice to your friends, okay?

00:11:57.180 --> 00:12:01.210
Know what happened around here in middle school?

00:12:01.210 --> 00:12:02.450
Just some rumors.

00:12:03.640 --> 00:12:06.120
I was trying to pick a fight,

00:12:08.420 --> 00:12:13.410
but alone I just kinda lacked the confidence.

00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:19.160
Having Yamato there made a huge difference.

00:12:27.370 --> 00:12:30.130
Too bad he got your crush.

00:12:30.130 --> 00:12:31.750
I'm fine with that if it's Yamato.

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:33.860
Really now?

00:12:33.860 --> 00:12:35.330
Think you'll get a boyfriend with that attitude?

00:12:37.130 --> 00:12:38.290
Yes?

00:12:38.290 --> 00:12:40.110
Yeah, it changed.

00:12:40.110 --> 00:12:40.940
3 PM now.

00:12:41.350 --> 00:12:42.640
I'm fine.

00:12:42.640 --> 00:12:44.370
Thank you.

00:12:44.370 --> 00:12:45.620
Yes.

00:12:45.620 --> 00:12:46.960
Goodbye.

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:57.090
You seem busy.

00:12:57.090 --> 00:12:59.880
Is being a model that big a deal?{some kind of specific model, dont know terminology used}

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:01.620
How do you know about that?

00:13:01.620 --> 00:13:02.740
I saw you on some magazine cover.

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:04.740
Oh? Interested in fashion?

00:13:04.740 --> 00:13:06.300
Just saw it in a store.

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:07.450
You didn't buy it?

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:11.050
Popularity is fragile.

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:14.890
Keeping it alive is difficult, and there are other things I want to do as well.

00:13:15.660 --> 00:13:17.200
I'm not done.

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:21.970
I don't know much about that, but hang in there.

00:13:21.970 --> 00:13:23.400
It must be a lot of stress.

00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:24.810
Yeah, it is.

00:13:25.460 --> 00:13:29.040
But I want to stick this out while still being myself.

00:13:30.650 --> 00:13:32.770
I didn't need you for that, though.

00:13:33.650 --> 00:13:35.080
Sounds cool.

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:36.290
Are you making fun of me?

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:38.130
Huh? I'm super serious here.

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:38.740
I know you're lying.

00:13:38.740 --> 00:13:40.050
Take this seriously too.

00:13:40.050 --> 00:13:42.090
Drop the attitude then!

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:44.020
Who's the one with an attitude here?

00:13:44.020 --> 00:13:44.910
What, me?

00:13:44.910 --> 00:13:46.270
But you're the one who...

00:13:47.290 --> 00:13:48.550
God, you piss me off.

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:49.050
What?

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:50.680
Are you ever gonna leave?

00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:51.570
Huh?

00:13:51.570 --> 00:13:53.340
Don't you have anything to do?

00:13:53.340 --> 00:13:56.530
I'm working here, so go flip burgers or something.

00:13:56.530 --> 00:13:58.020
What the fuck?

00:13:59.200 --> 00:14:00.480
What the hell is wrong with you?

00:14:03.180 --> 00:14:03.870
Jesus.

00:14:05.920 --> 00:14:07.780
The best of luck with your work.

00:14:31.020 --> 00:14:32.180
This is so heavy!

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:34.170
You look important!{i dont really understand these two lines, i think they stole something from that official-looking place in the background, but i dont get it}

00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:44.510
He pisses me off.

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:47.840
Megu!

00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:48.850
I'm sorry!

00:14:48.850 --> 00:14:50.730
I had the wrong bag with me.

00:14:50.730 --> 00:14:51.820
You're late!

00:14:51.820 --> 00:14:53.850
It's your fault, Momo.

00:14:53.850 --> 00:14:55.680
Who the hell does he think he is?

00:14:55.680 --> 00:14:59.280
He doesn't know anything and says all that bullshit.

00:14:59.280 --> 00:15:00.520
Who did you talk to?

00:15:00.520 --> 00:15:01.780
Takemura Kai.

00:15:01.780 --> 00:15:03.710
Oh, him.

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:05.650
I can't deal with him.

00:15:05.650 --> 00:15:07.370
Why did he start chatting me up?

00:15:07.370 --> 00:15:08.990
What'd I do to deserve that?

00:15:08.990 --> 00:15:10.100
Did you do something?

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:14.890
I don't know.

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:18.750
I don't understand him at all.

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:26.090
Do you love him?

00:15:26.090 --> 00:15:27.680
What?

00:15:28.750 --> 00:15:31.570
You don't normally talk about people like that.

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:32.740
Like what?

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:36.030
You might be putting on a front, or maybe... you might be trying to seem cooler?

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:38.130
Why would I do that with him?

00:15:38.130 --> 00:15:41.120
I think you'd make a cute couple, though.

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:42.120
What?!

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:43.840
Let's find a place to hang out, the three of us.

00:15:43.840 --> 00:15:44.720
Why?!

00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:46.020
It'll be fun!

00:15:46.020 --> 00:15:49.950
An odd number is kinda harsh, so let's reel someone else in.

00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:50.950
Please, no.

00:15:52.830 --> 00:15:54.700
I said something mean to him.

00:15:54.700 --> 00:15:56.090
Let's go apologize, then.

00:15:56.090 --> 00:15:58.060
If you can't say it to his face, send him a text.

00:15:58.060 --> 00:15:59.680
I don't have his number.

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:00.950
Let's go ask him.

00:16:00.950 --> 00:16:03.410
We could just straight up apologize then!

00:16:03.410 --> 00:16:05.010
Then let's go.

00:16:05.010 --> 00:16:07.150
I wonder where he lives.

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:08.570
I don't know!

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:09.540
I'm not going!

00:16:09.540 --> 00:16:11.490
No way in hell I'm going!

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:28.070
Please stop!

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:31.150
Why'd I get off the bus, I wonder.

00:16:35.100 --> 00:16:36.480
Please wait!

00:16:36.480 --> 00:16:37.730
I want on!

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:49.020
{part c}

00:16:50.150 --> 00:16:53.860
The long-awaited food tasting!

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:58.030
I tried my utmost to make it palatable.

00:17:11.980 --> 00:17:14.680
They're a bit fragile!

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:15.730
Be gentle.

00:17:16.410 --> 00:17:17.700
Thanks for the cookies.

00:17:27.810 --> 00:17:28.850
They're great!

00:17:28.850 --> 00:17:30.360
They're great, Mei!

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:31.150
Really?

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:32.350
Really really?

00:17:32.350 --> 00:17:33.680
You didn't try yourself?

00:17:33.680 --> 00:17:34.600
I did, but—

00:17:34.600 --> 00:17:36.400
Good job, Mei!

00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:37.310
Thanks.

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:41.940
It's no surprise they're good when I told her what to do.

00:17:41.940 --> 00:17:43.000
Nagisa...

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:45.960
Thank you.

00:17:47.550 --> 00:17:49.540
Yup, they're good.

00:18:01.230 --> 00:18:03.140
Thank you so much.

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:04.660
You had to come all the way here.

00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:05.930
No, I should thank you.

00:18:06.330 --> 00:18:08.610
Takeshi will like some cookies too.

00:18:08.610 --> 00:18:10.980
It was fun making them.

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:13.230
It was, wasn't it?

00:18:13.230 --> 00:18:14.530
Let's do it again.

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:15.440
I'd love to.

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:19.130
What? Mei's got a boyfriend?

00:18:19.130 --> 00:18:21.780
It's my brother, so don't worry.

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:22.200
Nagi.

00:18:22.720 --> 00:18:24.390
Wait until we're done here.

00:18:24.390 --> 00:18:25.520
We're making quiche.

00:18:25.520 --> 00:18:26.180
Right?

00:18:26.180 --> 00:18:27.040
Right.

00:18:29.760 --> 00:18:32.080
Could you go buy something to drink, Mei?

00:18:32.080 --> 00:18:33.630
And take Yamato with.

00:18:34.380 --> 00:18:36.320
I want something carbonated.

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:45.640
I'm sorry if Nagi messed up your kitchen.

00:18:47.430 --> 00:18:49.600
I think Mom was having fun too.

00:18:50.680 --> 00:18:51.870
I...

00:18:52.960 --> 00:18:54.230
I had fun too.

00:18:55.150 --> 00:18:59.530
They others said they had fun too.

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:04.930
The kitchen was a lot more lively than usual.

00:19:07.420 --> 00:19:09.080
Having people around can be so nice.

00:19:17.310 --> 00:19:19.060
I felt lonely without you.

00:19:19.060 --> 00:19:22.270
I'm really sorry about that.

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:35.650
I'm sorry.

00:19:41.500 --> 00:19:42.480
Thanks.

00:19:43.760 --> 00:19:45.330
I'm really happy I met you.

00:19:48.720 --> 00:19:50.580
Why're you saying this now?

00:19:51.140 --> 00:19:52.270
No reason in particular.

00:19:53.590 --> 00:19:54.470
Wait.

00:19:54.470 --> 00:19:55.300
I'm worried!

00:19:55.300 --> 00:19:56.330
Are you okay?

00:19:56.330 --> 00:19:58.680
Is there something you want to tell me?

00:19:58.680 --> 00:20:00.030
Nothing I haven't told you.

00:20:13.050 --> 00:20:14.030
So beautiful.

00:20:27.680 --> 00:20:28.870
Yeah.

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:35.670
You might be the reason.

00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:15.670
